Product Requirement Document (PRD): Fleet Operations Platform

1. Project Overview & Architecture

Purpose: Centralized internal operational platform for multi-hub electric vehicle (EV) fleet management, maintenance lifecycle tracking, multi-location spare parts inventory, approval workflows, multi-tiered task delegation, and non-destructive audit logging.

Tech Stack:

Frontend: Next.js 14+ (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, Lucide Icons (Responsive layout for mobile field staff & desktop command center).

Backend & Database: Supabase (PostgreSQL, Supabase Auth, Row-Level Security, Database Triggers/Stored Procedures, Storage Buckets for photo attachments).

State Management & Fetching: TanStack React Query v5, Zustand, React Hook Form + Zod.

2. Dynamic RBAC & Multi-Role Architecture

Users can hold multiple roles simultaneously. Effective permissions are computed additively ($\text{Role}_A \cup \text{Role}_B$).

2.1 Default System Roles

Owner (Admin): Full system access, approval overrides, role configuration, master audits, and settings.

Manager: Hub assignment, task allocation, job card approvals, spare part usage sign-offs, refund verification, and vehicle status management.

RSA (Roadside Assistance): Field breakdown reporting, towing/battery swap logs, roadside repair execution, and field expense logging.

Mechanic: Maintenance log entry, defect diagnosis, spare parts allocation requests, and digital vehicle checklist audits.

