-- 7. Immutable Audit Trail (Zero Hard Deletes)
CREATE TABLE audit_logs (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
    table_name TEXT NOT NULL,
    record_id UUID NOT NULL,
    action TEXT NOT NULL, -- 'INSERT', 'UPDATE', 'SOFT_DELETE'
    performed_by UUID REFERENCES profiles(id) ON DELETE RESTRICT,
    old_data JSONB,
    new_data JSONB,
    timestamp TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);


4. Operational Invariants & Approval Logic

4.1 Two-Phase Inventory Staging Rule

Available Stock Calculation:


$$\text{Available Stock} = \text{Physical Stock} - \text{Pending Allocated Stock}$$

UI Pattern: Available (Physical)

Example: 14 units on the shelf, 4 units logged by mechanic on pending job card $\rightarrow$ Displayed as 10 (14).

State Lifecycle:

Part Requested: Mechanic adds 4 brake pads to a Job Card $\rightarrow$ hub_parts_stock.pending_allocated_stock increments by 4. Physical stock remains 14. UI reads 10 (14).

Job Card Approved: Manager clicks "Approve" $\rightarrow$ hub_parts_stock.physical_stock decrements by 4, pending_allocated_stock decrements by 4. UI reads 10 (10).

4.2 Two-Phase Vehicle Status Staging Rule

When a field technician reports a defect, they update pending_status = 'UNDER_REPAIR'.

UI Pattern: Current Status (Pending: Staged Status) (e.g., AVAILABLE (Pending: UNDER_REPAIR)).

Upon Manager/Owner approval: current_status updates to UNDER_REPAIR, and pending_status resets to NULL.

4.3 Zero Hard Deletes & Audit Trigger

Hard DELETE operations are strictly blocked via PostgreSQL triggers.

Soft deletions set is_active = FALSE.

Every mutation executes an AFTER UPDATE trigger creating a JSON diff record in audit_logs.

-- Audit Trigger Function
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION process_audit_log()
RETURNS TRIGGER AS $$
BEGIN
    INSERT INTO audit_logs (table_name, record_id, action, performed_by, old_data, new_data)
    VALUES (
        TG_TABLE_NAME,
        COALESCE(NEW.id, OLD.id),
        TG_OP,
        auth.uid(),
        to_jsonb(OLD),
        to_jsonb(NEW)
    );
    RETURN NEW;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql SECURITY DEFINER;

-- Attach triggers to core operational tables
CREATE TRIGGER audit_vehicles AFTER UPDATE ON vehicles FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION process_audit_log();
CREATE TRIGGER audit_job_cards AFTER UPDATE ON job_cards FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION process_audit_log();
CREATE TRIGGER audit_hub_stock AFTER UPDATE ON hub_parts_stock FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION process_audit_log();
CREATE TRIGGER audit_refunds AFTER UPDATE ON refunds FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION process_audit_log();


5. UI/UX & Screen Breakdown

5.1 Mobile Field Interface (RSA & Mechanics)

Vehicle Scanner & Lookup: Search via plate number or QR to view live battery, key number, and full repair history.

Maintenance Job Logger:

Multi-step form: Select vehicle $\rightarrow$ checklist of issues $\rightarrow$ take/upload photos $\rightarrow$ multi-select spare parts from current hub stock $\rightarrow$ Submit.

Field Task View: Filtered list of assigned tasks under active objectives with quick-toggle status (TODO $\rightarrow$ COMPLETED).

5.2 Desktop Operations Dashboard (Managers & Owners)

Approvals Desk (Priority Queue):

Pending Job Cards (view issue, photos, parts requested, and total cost impact).

Vehicle Status Transitions (approve/reject state changes).

Refund Verification Queue (view ride ID, reason, amount, and proof).

Hub Directory & Fleet Grid:

Hub list with POC details, security contacts, active charging ports, and assigned vehicle counts.

Vehicle Master Sheet: Filterable table with deep-dive modal showing chronological vehicle lifecycle logs.

Objective & Task Management (Hierarchical To-Do):

Set top-level Objective (e.g., "Hub 2 Fleet Overhaul - Target: Friday") $\rightarrow$ Create child tasks assigned to specific mechanics/RSAs.

Inventory Master:

Matrix of parts across all hubs showing Available (Physical) counts with red highlight triggers when available stock falls below min_threshold.

6. AI Implementation Prompt (Copy-Paste Ready)

Build a responsive Next.js 14+ (App Router) internal operations platform with Supabase (PostgreSQL, Auth, Storage) and Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui.

Key Requirements:
1. Setup dynamic multi-role RBAC (Owner, Manager, RSA, Mechanic) supporting multiple roles per user.
2. Implement two-phase staging for inventory and vehicle status:
   - Inventory UI: Show "Available (Physical)" stock (e.g., 10 (14)). Available = Physical - Pending. Decrement physical stock only upon manager approval of job cards.
   - Vehicle UI: Show "Current (Pending: Target)" status when a state change is submitted by field staff until signed off.
3. Build complete interlinked vehicle history logs: Opening a vehicle detail view must display all historical job cards, parts consumed with unit costs, mechanics involved, and audit logs.
4. Implement a hierarchical To-Do engine: Objectives (assigned to hubs) containing nested Tasks (assigned to personnel with priorities and optional vehicle links).
5. Enforce zero hard deletes: Block SQL DELETE and log full JSON diffs on every update to an immutable audit_logs table.
6. Provide a mobile-optimized view for RSA/Mechanics (ticket logging, camera uploads, task completion) and a desktop dashboard for Managers/Owners (Approvals Desk, Fleet Grid, Stock Matrix).

